---
import { sitePath } from '../lib/links';
interface Props {
  file: string;
  events: string;
}
const { file, events } = Astro.props;
---

<p>
  Start with <a href={sitePath('getting-started/')}>Your first sound</a> if you have not set up a
  sound scene before. Use a separate test scene with <strong>one enabled Sound Manager</strong>,
  generated Sound Keys, and <strong>one Audio Listener</strong> near the sound object. Add{' '}
  <strong>{events}</strong> to the manager's <strong>Direct events</strong> list; these are the
  supplied <code>.soundgraph</code> assets under <code>Assets/DEV505/SoundManager/Samples</code>.
</p>
<p>
  Save the complete code below as <strong>{file}</strong> in <code>Assets/Scripts</code>. Wait for
  Unity to compile it, create an empty GameObject, and drag the script onto it. The filename must
  match the class name. Test one recipe component at a time so another demo controller does not
  compete for the same events.
</p>
<slot />
<p>
  In Play Mode, wait until the Sound Manager is ready. To run a listed test action, open the
  component's three-dot menu in the Inspector and choose that action. These are the script's{' '}
  <code>ContextMenu</code> methods. Your own code or a Unity UI Button can call its public methods
  too. Inspector edits made during Play Mode are temporary.
</p>
